Cloud modernization goes beyond simply moving existing applications to Azure. It involves improving applications and infrastructure so that organizations can take advantage of cloud-native capabilities.

Modernization approaches include:

* Rehosting
* Refactoring
* Rearchitecting
* Rebuilding
* Replacing legacy systems

For example, a legacy application running on physical servers can initially be rehosted on Azure virtual machines. Later, components may be migrated to Azure App Service, containers, managed databases, or serverless services.

A real-life use case is an enterprise gradually transforming a decades-old application into a modern cloud-native platform without attempting a complete rewrite immediately.

Cloud modernization improves scalability, agility, maintainability, and long-term business value.
